WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:06.809
In the Game of Thrones books, Tyrion Lannister
is a fan of Lomas Longstrider – an adventurer

00:00:06.809 --> 00:00:08.970
who travelled [round] the world.

00:00:08.970 --> 00:00:14.469
Lomas wrote books about the wonders he saw
– and named nine wonders made by man . They

00:00:14.469 --> 00:00:19.700
include the Wall in the north, the Titan of
Braavos , the bells of Norvos, the Bridge

00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:25.750
of Volantis, the roads of Valyria, the Palace
of Sarnath and the walls of Qarth.

00:00:25.750 --> 00:00:30.960
That’s seven wonders, so there should be
two more – and fans have speculated on what

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:32.279
they could be.

00:00:32.279 --> 00:00:37.120
So what are the wonders of the world of Game
of Thrones?

00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:41.989
The Wall is huge wall of ice that divides
the kingdoms of Westeros from the wildlings

00:00:41.989 --> 00:00:43.059
in the north.

00:00:43.059 --> 00:00:47.910
Author George Martin says this was inspired
by Hadrian’s Wall, which divided Roman Britain

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:52.600
from the Scots in the north – in fact George
pretty much copied the map.

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:57.780
But Hadrian’s Wall was only seventy miles
long – Martin’s wall is three hundred

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:03.070
miles long , and up to seven hundred feet
tall , which is half an Empire State , or

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:09.180
two Big Bens , or over a hundred Hodors tall
. According to legend, the Wall was built

00:01:09.180 --> 00:01:13.890
thousands of years ago by humans and giants
and the children of the forest , to keep out

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:19.130
the white walkers . But some fans believe
that the Wall was built by the walkers, maybe

00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:22.079
part of an agreement with the humans.

00:01:22.079 --> 00:01:28.850
So the Wall is ancient and magic and mysterious
– Melisandre says it’s “one of the hinges

00:01:28.850 --> 00:01:33.700
of the world” . She says “If the Wall
falls”, there’ll be a “night that never

00:01:33.700 --> 00:01:38.510
ends” . And in Season 7 of the show, the
Wall falls.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:43.799
In the books, the Wall still stands, but there
is this magic horn with the power to “break”

00:01:43.799 --> 00:01:50.060
the Wall – go watch that video .
The next wonder is the Titan of Braavos.

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:54.670
The Titan is a “fortress” “in the shape
of a warrior”, who stands across the entrance

00:01:54.670 --> 00:02:00.409
to Braavos . He’s carved of stone, with
bronze armor, and long hair made of green

00:02:00.409 --> 00:02:06.759
ropes . The Titan’s eyes blaze with fires
to light the way for incoming ships – and

00:02:06.759 --> 00:02:09.470
to intimidate invaders.

00:02:09.470 --> 00:02:15.430
Inside the Titan are rooms with arrow-slits
– defenders can drop stones, and burning

00:02:15.430 --> 00:02:16.430
pitch.

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:20.710
It’s said that if Braavos is attacked, the
Titan will come to life, wade out to sea,

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:25.620
and smash his enemies – but for hundreds
of years, no invader has been brave enough

00:02:25.620 --> 00:02:31.530
to attack . The Titan makes a loud roaring
sound every sunrise and sunset , and people

00:02:31.530 --> 00:02:37.340
keep track of time by its roar . Each year,
Braavos has a festival where everyone wears

00:02:37.340 --> 00:02:43.050
masks, and at midnight, the Titan roars and
everyone takes off their masks together – the

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:46.960
Titan is a symbol of pride for the people
of Braavos.

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:51.810
The Titan might be inspired by the Colossus
of Rhodes, a statue who guarded the Greek

00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:56.141
island thousands of years ago .
Next are the bells of Norvos.

00:02:56.141 --> 00:03:03.670
Norvos is an eastern city known for its bears
and axes . It’s ruled by the bearded priests,

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:09.890
a sect so mysterious that even the name of
their god is secret . But their religion runs

00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:13.140
the city – with these three bells.

00:03:13.140 --> 00:03:18.570
Their ringing tells the Norvosi when to wake,
when to sleep, to work rest and pray, and

00:03:18.570 --> 00:03:20.530
even when to have sex.

00:03:20.530 --> 00:03:27.080
The bells are named Noom, Narrah, and Nyel,
each with its own distinct voice . Areo Hotah

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:33.460
is from Norvos, and his memories of the bells
remind him of home . The bells of Norvos sounding

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:39.240
the time to pray might be inspired by Islamic
and Christian calls to prayer .

00:03:39.240 --> 00:03:42.400
The next wonder is the roads of Valyria.

00:03:42.400 --> 00:03:45.710
Valyria was an empire of the ancient dragonlords.

00:03:45.710 --> 00:03:51.870
They ruled a huge chunk of the world , and
bound it together with sorcery and technology.

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:58.010
They used dragonflame to melt and fuse stone,
shaping it into structures stronger than steel

00:03:58.010 --> 00:04:04.090
. And with this dragon-stone, they built a
network of long, straight roads, from Valyria

00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:06.360
to Volantis to Meereen.

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:11.210
This helped transport trade and armies – extending
the dragonlords’ reach.

00:04:11.210 --> 00:04:15.750
Four hundred years ago, Valyria was destroyed
in an apocalyptic Doom.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:19.250
The dragonlords died, and their cities collapsed.

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:25.420
But their roads remain – unmarred and unchanged,
four centuries later . It’s like how some

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:29.270
roads of ancient Rome remain today.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:32.000
Next is the Long Bridge of Volantis.

00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.990
Volantis was founded by the Valyrians as a
military outpost on the river Rhoyne . It

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:41.970
grew into a town on the east bank – while
on the west bank, a “shadow city” grew,

00:04:41.970 --> 00:04:47.960
attracting criminals and vice . It was difficult
to cross between these two halves of Volantis,

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:51.410
so the city was united with the Long Bridge.

00:04:51.410 --> 00:04:56.540
It took forty years and millions of honors,
but they constructed the biggest bridge in

00:04:56.540 --> 00:05:02.100
the world – said to be able to hold a thousand
elephants . There are buildings on the bridge

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.060
– shops, temples, taverns and brothels.

00:05:05.060 --> 00:05:10.710
They’re stacked three or four stories tall,
leaning inwards, so crossing the bridge feels

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:15.970
like going through a tunnel . It’s said
you “can buy most anything on the Long Bridge”

00:05:15.970 --> 00:05:21.820
– from gloves to monkeys to slaves . The
Long Bridge in the show is based on a real

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:24.660
Roman bridge in Spain.

00:05:24.660 --> 00:05:29.500
In the grasslands of Essos, there was once
a kingdom called Sarnor, whose “gleaming

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:35.080
cities were strewn across the grasslands like
jewels across … green velvet” . The “greatest

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.981
of these cities was Sarnath”, “where the
High King dwelt” in a fabled “Palace With

00:05:39.981 --> 00:05:45.810
a Thousand Rooms” . We don’t know anything
about this Palace, but eventually Sarnath

00:05:45.810 --> 00:05:52.090
was destroyed by the Dothraki – the Palace
was burned , and Sarnath renamed the “City

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:53.730
of Worms”.

00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:59.540
Hundreds of years later, in Book 1, Daenerys
passes its ruins on her way through the Dothraki

00:05:59.540 --> 00:06:03.210
Sea .
In Book 2, Daenerys visits Qarth.

00:06:03.210 --> 00:06:09.030
It’s a “city of splendors” , with colourful
buildings, fountains and towers, and archways

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:15.250
decorated with gems . But the wonder of Qarth
is its triple walls – the three layers of

00:06:15.250 --> 00:06:17.830
walls that encircle the city.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:23.660
The outer wall is red sandstone, decorated
with carvings of animals – snakes, elephants,

00:06:23.660 --> 00:06:25.860
wolves and zorses.

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:31.870
The middle walls are grey granite, carved
with scenes of war – clashing swords, heroes

00:06:31.870 --> 00:06:34.770
at battle, pyres of the dead.

00:06:34.770 --> 00:06:40.810
And the inner wall is black marble, carved
with scenes of sex that make Dany blush . These

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:47.250
triple walls protected Qarth from the Sarnori
and Dothraki – leaving Qarth the last surviving

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:52.780
city of the Qaathi people .
So these are the seven known wonders – but

00:06:52.780 --> 00:06:55.470
Lomas Longstrider listed nine.

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:59.930
Fans have speculated on what his other two
could be.

00:06:59.930 --> 00:07:04.800
The Hightower in Oldtown is “the tallest
structure in the Seven Kingdoms” – even

00:07:04.800 --> 00:07:09.840
taller than the Wall . It’s a lighthouse
to guide ships into port, but it’s also

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:12.930
a castle, home to House Hightower.

00:07:12.930 --> 00:07:18.780
The Hightower is mysterious cause it’s built
on top of an ancient fortress of strange black

00:07:18.780 --> 00:07:26.270
stone so old that no one knows who built it
. The stone seems fused like dragonstone , but

00:07:26.270 --> 00:07:31.580
the style of the building doesn’t seem Valyrian
. So some maesters say it was built by the

00:07:31.580 --> 00:07:38.070
mazemakers of Lorath , or by the Lovecraftian
Deep Ones . Or maybe it was the Great Empire

00:07:38.070 --> 00:07:39.389
of the Dawn.

00:07:39.389 --> 00:07:44.950
Whatever its strange origins, the Hightower
is impressive, and could be one of Lomas’

00:07:44.950 --> 00:07:45.950
wonders.

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:50.770
The Hightower’s inspired by the Lighthouse
of Alexandria – but George made it twice

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:54.710
as tall .
Another possible wonder is the Great Pyramid

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:55.710
of Ghis.

00:07:55.710 --> 00:07:58.139
Ghis was an ancient slave city.

00:07:58.139 --> 00:08:03.670
And their Great Pyramid was “colossal”
– thirty-three levels high, with red marble

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:05.580
halls inside.

00:08:05.580 --> 00:08:10.960
Five thousand years ago, Valyria conquered
Ghis, and burned their city, leaving the Pyramid

00:08:10.960 --> 00:08:12.370
in ruins.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:17.020
But descendants of Ghis founded the cities
of Slaver’s Bay – and the Great Pyramid

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:21.240
of Meereen was built as an “echo” of the
Pyramid of Ghis.

00:08:21.240 --> 00:08:27.580
So five thousand years after the fall of Ghis,
Daenerys still struggles to erase its legacy

00:08:27.580 --> 00:08:29.330
of slavery.

00:08:29.330 --> 00:08:35.510
Lomas Longstrider did visit the ruined Pyramid
in Ghis , so maybe it’s one of his wonders.

00:08:35.510 --> 00:08:37.860
Another possibility is the cities of Yi Ti.

00:08:37.860 --> 00:08:45.240
Yi Ti is a great empire inspired by China
. Lomas visited Yi Ti, and was “awestruck

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:50.710
by its marvels” . He said its cities are
far larger and more magnificent than any in

00:08:50.710 --> 00:08:56.450
Westeros – that “Even their ruins” put
Westerosi cities “to shame” . The current

00:08:56.450 --> 00:09:01.980
emperor of Yi Ti lives in a palace that’s
even bigger than all of King’s Landing – so

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.100
that might be one of Lomas’s wonders.

00:09:05.100 --> 00:09:09.500
Finally, beyond Yi Ti, are the Five Forts.

00:09:09.500 --> 00:09:15.380
These mysterious, ancient fortresses are described
as “godlike” and “demonic”.

00:09:15.380 --> 00:09:20.080
Each Fort “is large enough to house ten
thousand men”, and “their massive walls

00:09:20.080 --> 00:09:25.040
stand almost a thousand feet high” – all
built of fused black dragonstone.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.170
We don’t know if Lomas made it this far
east.

00:09:29.170 --> 00:09:35.630
But if he saw the Forts, he must have thought
them wonderous – or “monstrous”.

00:09:35.630 --> 00:09:39.520
So these are the wonders of the world of Game
of Thrones.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:43.810
Author George Martin basically nicked them
from the real world – took Hadrian’s Wall

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:48.310
and Rhodes’ Colossus and Alexandria’s
Lighthouse and just made’m bigger and bit

00:09:48.310 --> 00:09:49.520
magic.

00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:54.740
So this shows not only of the wonders of Game
of Thrones – but it’s a reminder of the

00:09:54.740 --> 00:09:57.610
wonders of our own world.

